The '''Iyika''' ({{Langx|kz|ߌߦߌߞߊ|Ìyíká|revolutionaries}}) serve as the decentralized [[W:Army|ground defense force]] of the [[Sanyan|State of Sanyan]], dedicated to protecting the city-state’s territories. Operating autonomously within the broader framework of the [[Sanyan Defense Force]], their organization reflects a unique communal structure. Each unit of the Iyika operates within a clearly defined area, most often corresponding to their respective [[Communes of Sanyan|commune]]. Coordination is managed by the local defense committee, which oversees the activities of these cadres and receives weekly reports from the group secretaries.

Unlike traditional military forces, Iyika volunteers do not adhere to hierarchical formalities such as saluting superiors or performing ceremonial duties. Officers are elected and can be swiftly replaced if necessary, ensuring dynamic leadership. Furthermore, all members have the right to discuss and debate orders, executing them only if they collectively agree, reflecting the Iyika's emphasis on communal decision-making and participatory governance.

